   "text": "```python\n\"\"\"\nlru_ttl_cache.py\n\nA comprehensive, thread-safe, LRU (Least Recently Used) cache implementation\nthat supports Time-To-Live (TTL) expiration. This module provides both a\npublic API for usage and an internal implementation suitable for production\nenvironments where data consistency, thread safety, and memory management\nare critical.\n\nKey Features:\n    - LRU eviction policy based on access time.\n    - TTL expiration based on set expiration time.\n    - Thread-safe operations using internal locking.\n    - Support for custom key serializers.\n    - Integration with asyncio for async environments.\n    - Extensive test suite using pytest to validate correctness, performance,\n      and edge cases.\n\nUsage Example:\n    from lru_ttl_cache import LruTtlCache\n\n    cache = LruTtlCache(maxsize=100, ttl_seconds=3600)\n    cache.set(\"key1\", value1, ttl=10)\n    cache.set(\"key2\", value2, ttl=5)\n    print(cache.get(\"key1\"))  # Returns value1\n    print(cache.get(\"key2\"))  # Returns value2 after 5 seconds, then None\n\n    # Eviction example\n    cache.set(\"key3\", value3, ttl=100)\n    # Access key3\n    cache.get(\"key3\")\n    # Evict another key, key2 will be evicted\n    cache.set(\"key4\", value4, ttl=100)\n\nAuthor: AI Assistant\nVersion: 1.0.0\nLicense: MIT\n\"\"\"\n\nimport time\nimport threading\nimport asyncio\nimport functools\nimport weakref\nfrom typing import (\n    Any,\n    Dict,\n    Optional,\n    TypeVar,\n    Generic,\n    Callable,\n    List,\n    Tuple,\n    Union,\n    Iterator,\n    Iterable,\n    Set,\n    FrozenSet,\n    TYPE_CHECKING,\n)\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom enum import Enum\nimport copy\nimport json\nimport hashlib\nimport logging\nimport sys\nimport traceback\n\n# Configure logging for internal tracing\nlogging.basicConfig(\n    level=logging.DEBUG,\n    format=\"%(asctime)s [%(levelname)s] %(message)s\"\n)\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name",
